## Summary of changes

- **Added `-m`/`--mode` parsing**: Supports `-m MODE`, `-mMODE`, `--mode MODE`, `--mode=MODE`. Last occurrence wins.
- **Added `_parse_mode()`**: Handles numeric octal (0–7777) and symbolic modes.
- **Added symbolic mode engine** (`_apply_clause`, `_apply_regular`, `_apply_copy`): Implements GNU 9.11 semantics with:
  - Starting mode = `0o777 & ~umask`
  - `a=rwx` as the `=` reference (not umask-reduced)
  - Umask filtering only for omitted-who `+`/`-`/`=` on ordinary bits
  - Special bit rules: `s`→setuid(u)/setgid(g), `t`→sticky(o/a/omitted)
  - `=` preserves setuid/setgid unless explicitly addressed; clears sticky unless explicitly set
  - Permission copy (`u+g`, etc.)
  - `X` treated as `x` (always directories)
  - Empty assignments (`o=`) valid
- **Modified `_create_dir()`**: Applies exact mode via `chmod` after creation when `-m` is specified.
- **Modified `_create_dir_p()`**: Intermediates get `(0o777 & ~umask) | 0o300`; final directory gets the parsed mode (or default). Existing directories untouched.
- **Mode validation** happens before any filesystem operations.
- **Options parsed globally** (before/after operands), all applying to all operands.
